$ ./run.sh --help
usage: floscan run [-h] --input INPUT --tier {photo,video,lidar} --output
                   OUTPUT --mode {live,replay} [--gates GATES]

Process one capture directory at an explicitly declared tier and write OUTPUT/result.json. This build implements no reconstruction: it inventories the input and writes a validated diagnostic envelope that reports every unavailable section.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --input INPUT         capture directory (never modified)
  --tier {photo,video,lidar}
                        declared input tier; never auto-detected or upgraded
  --output OUTPUT       new result directory, outside the input; existing
                        results are kept
  --mode {live,replay}  live processes the raw input; replay only reuses a
                        matching cache
  --gates GATES         gate registry (default: configs/gates.yaml)

exit codes:
  0  ok: the full output contract was produced (not reachable in this build)
  1  failed: internal error, invalid gate registry, invalid envelope,
     or a filesystem error reading the input or writing the result; no result
  2  usage error: bad arguments, unknown tier, output inside input,
     or an existing result (run directories are append-only); nothing written
  3  invalid_input: input missing, not a directory or empty; envelope written
  4  incomplete: envelope written, output contract not produced
  5  replay unavailable: no matching replay cache; live inference not attempted
